WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
BUILD 027. POSTING IS NOT OWNERSHIP. A platform can distribute the work without giving you control of the audience, archive, identity, or future access.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY. NAME WHAT YOU ACTUALLY OWN. Track source files, authorship, licenses, collaborators, permissions, registrations, and every reused component.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
AUDIENCE. BUILD A DIRECT RELATIONSHIP. Consent-based email, portable contacts, preference history, and clear unsubscribe routes survive an algorithm change.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
INFRASTRUCTURE. KEEP THE CANONICAL COPY. Use your domain, durable archive, structured metadata, exports, backups, and migration paths as the source of truth.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
DISTRIBUTION. LET PLATFORMS BE CHANNELS. Syndicate outward, measure dependencies, preserve attribution, and keep a tested exit for every critical service.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
SAVE THIS. REACH IS NOT CONTROL. PLATFORM REACH IS RENTED. YOUR OWNERSHIP STACK MUST SURVIVE THE PLATFORM.

